	(wire (pts (xy 297.18 180.34) (xy 312.42 180.34)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "7939fc03-804c-49c3-bfcd-52efaadb6c72"))
	(global_label "SWDIO_NRF" (shape bidirectional) (at 312.42 180.34 0) (fields_autoplaced yes)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "d077f6a4-f9fc-4fd1-847e-82c1b0ebc305")
		(property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}" (at 312.42 180.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
	)
	(text "SWDIO goes both ways, so it gets the classic MOSFET level-shifter: gate at V3, drain toward the pad.\nEither side pulling low turns the FET on and pulls the other side low. Pad at 5 V (key bridge): the\nsource can only rise to V3 - Vth, the FET turns off and R606 holds the nRF pin at V3. It never\nexceeds V3, injects nothing into V3, and needs no firmware." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 204 137 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5c7fa4e6-cfe5-45fc-b574-4b64643847a0"))
	(text "When the nRF drives SWDIO high, the FET is off: the DOCK must pull its side up to VTref\n(dock-board requirement, ~10 k). R606 4.7 k gives ~120 ns edges -> SWD at 2 MHz is\ncomfortable, 4 MHz marginal (EV-9). Use 2.2 k if 4 MHz is needed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 204 200 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cff76244-15ce-44da-b841-953f625763d9"))
	(rectangle (start 15 160) (end 190 262) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash) (color 72 72 72 1)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "78cb617f-74d0-47fd-8a83-b7ec4e41cdef"))
	(text "D · What the dock board must provide (report A.2 + this sheet)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 16.5 161.5 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d238e611-020f-4a71-8a8f-819a18a64078"))
	(text "1. 5 V to the VBUS pogo, current-limited: a key across the live pins must be harmless.\n2. 3.3 V LDO for VTref on the 10-pin Cortex debug header (the 4-wire head has no VTref).\n3. ~10 k pull-up from the SWDIO pogo to VTref (the limiter cell cannot drive the pad high).\n4. Mechanical keying of the cradle: a reversed head puts -5 V on the signal pads while a\n   programmer is attached (report F8) - survivable through 220R, but not harmless.\n5. Magnets in the head, 0.3 mm 430 shim in the device wall (no magnet in the device).\n\nBench jig for EVM-1 (report A.2): Adafruit 5412-class 4-pin magnetic cable rewired to a\nCortex header, VTref from a bench 3.3 V, keyed printed cradle." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 19 170 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ccf020ad-5b62-4c69-83f7-2ecbf3296118"))
	(text "Interfaces   out: VBUS_PAD (-> power), SWDCLK_NRF, SWDIO_NRF, DOCK_ID (-> nrf9151)   rails in: V3   Refs 6xx   [U] = part class chosen, MPN not final" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15 268 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d8cbc529-493f-43ed-b305-dfff62c80812"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
